* [[Tyler Hoechlin]] as [[Clark Kent (Superman & Lois)|Clark Kent / Superman]]:<br />A superhero from Krypton, and husband of Lois, who defends Earth.<ref name="SeriesAnnouncement" /> [[Dylan Kingwell]] portrays a teenage Clark in season one, Josh Zaharia portrays a teenage Clark in season two, Lennix James portrays a four-year-old Clark, Thomas Hoeving portrays Clark in his childhood, and Parker Cousineau portrays Clark in grade school. In an interview with [[Michael Rosenbaum]] on ''Inside of You'' following the series' finale, Hoechlin admitted that he accepted the part of Superman without fully understanding the character and that he had grown up being more of a fan of [[Batman]] and [[Indiana Jones]].
* [[Elizabeth Tulloch]] as [[Lois Lane (Superman & Lois)|Lois Lane]]: A journalist and wife of Clark.<ref name="SeriesAnnouncement" />
* Jordan Elsass (seasons 1–2) and Michael Bishop (seasons 3–4) as [[Jonathan Kent (Superman & Lois)|Jonathan Kent]]:<br />The modest, kind-hearted and athletic son of Clark and Lois who, unlike Jordan, initially did not inherit any Kryptonian superpowers, though they manifest after an emotional outburst in season 4. He is named after Clark's adoptive father, Jonathan Kent.<ref name="ElsassGarfin" /> Elsass departed the series prior to the third season due to personal issues, and the role was recast to Bishop.<ref name="ElsassExits">{{cite web|last=Murphy|first=J. Kim|title='Superman & Lois' Recasting Jonathan Kent as Jordan Elsass Exits Series|url=https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/superman-and-lois-jordan-elsass-exits-recast-1235343254/|website=Variety|date=August 16, 2022|access-date=August 16, 2022|archive-date=August 17, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220817013612/https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/superman-and-lois-jordan-elsass-exits-recast-1235343254/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Bishop">{{cite web|last=Petski|first=Denise|title='Superman & Lois': Michael Bishop To Play Jonathan Kent In Recasting In CW Series|url=https://deadline.com/2022/09/superman-lois-michael-bishop-jonathan-kent-recasting-cw-series-1235109618/|website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|date=September 7, 2022|access-date=September 7, 2022|url-status=live|archive-date=February 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204064503/https://deadline.com/2022/09/superman-lois-michael-bishop-jonathan-kent-recasting-cw-series-1235109618/}}</ref> Brady Droulis portrays a seven-year-old Jonathan Kent.
* [[Alex Garfin]] as Jordan Kent:<br />The introspective son of Clark and Lois, who is an outcast with social anxiety.<ref name="ElsassGarfin" /> Unlike Jonathan for the first 3 seasons, Jordan has inherited their father's powers, though early in season 1 his abilities only appear in "small bursts" but he manifests more powers and in season 2 he has grown powerful enough to fight Tal-Rho for a brief time. He is named after Clark's biological father, Jor-El. Dawson Littman portrays a seven-year-old Jordan Kent.
* [[Erik Valdez]] as Kyle Cushing (né Cortez):<br />Ex-husband of Lana Lang and Smallville's fire chief. Callous, abrasive, and a former alcoholic. A man always looking to do the right thing for the people he cares for. However, Cushing carries a chip on his shoulder about living in a small town.<ref name="Valdez" />
* [[Inde Navarrette]] as Sarah Cortez:<ref name="Holmes">{{cite web|last=Holmes|first=Adam|title=One Of Superman And Lois' Cut Leads Revealed Their Season 4 Return, But It's Not All Good News|url=https://www.cinemablend.com/superheroes/superman/superman-and-lois-cut-lead-inde-navarrette-sarah-cortez-season-4|website=Cinemablend|date=July 7, 2023|access-date=February 3, 2024|archive-date=February 3, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240203131727/https://www.cinemablend.com/superheroes/superman/superman-and-lois-cut-lead-inde-navarrette-sarah-cortez-season-4|url-status=live}}</ref><br />Kyle and Lana's "wild child" daughter who befriends the Kent boys and serves as Jordan's love interest.<ref name="Navarrette" /> In the season 2 episode "[[Girl... You'll Be A Woman, Soon]]" she celebrates her [[quinceañera]] and changes her name to Cortez, which was her family's name before they changed it.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.cbr.com/superman-lois-destroyed-lana-langs-family/|title=Superman & Lois Destroyed Lana Lang's Family|last=Matadeen|first=Renaldo|publisher=[[Comic Book Resources]]|access-date=February 28, 2022|date=February 27, 2022|archive-date=February 28, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220228084838/https://www.cbr.com/superman-lois-destroyed-lana-langs-family/|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[Wolé Parks]] as [[Steel (John Henry Irons)|John Henry Irons]]:<br />A soldier and talented engineer from an unidentified parallel Earth who is hellbent on proving to the world that it no longer needs Superman. He eventually accepts Superman as the savior of Earth and teams up with him to protect people from Morgan Edge.<ref name="Parks" />
* [[Adam Rayner]] as [[Morgan Edge (Superman & Lois)|Tal-Rho / Morgan Edge]] / [[Eradicator (character)|Eradicator]] (season 1; special guest season 2):<br />An "intelligent, eloquent, and impassioned self-made mogul whose innate ability to motivate is the means to his success and others' demise."<ref name="Rayner">{{cite web|last=Ramos|first=Dino-Ray|date=December 17, 2020|title='Superman & Lois' Adds 'Tyrant' Star Adam Rayner As Morgan Edge|url=https://deadline.com/2020/12/superman-and-lois-adam-rayner-as-series-regular-morgan-edge-the-cw-1234658041/|access-date=December 17, 2020|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|archive-date=December 17, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201217170205/https://deadline.com/2020/12/superman-and-lois-adam-rayner-as-series-regular-morgan-edge-the-cw-1234658041/|url-status=live}}</ref> He is later revealed to be Kal-El's half-brother known as Tal-Rho through Kal's mother Lara Lor-Van and Zeta-Rho with plans to restore the Kryptonian race.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.tvline.com/interviews/superman-and-lois-recap-season-1-episode-9-morgan-edge-brother-1234681374/|title=Superman & Lois' Erik Valdez Reacts to Kyle's Big Secret, Weighs In on That 'Poignant' Morgan Edge Reveal|magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]|last=Swift|first=Andy|date=June 8, 2021|access-date=August 20, 2021|archive-date=August 19, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210819141808/https://tvline.com/2021/06/08/superman-and-lois-recap-season-1-episode-9-morgan-edge-brother/amp/|url-status=live}}</ref> Jack Rehbein and Ben Cockell portray a 10-year-old Tal-Rho and a 19-year-old Tal-Rho, respectively.
* [[Dylan Walsh]] as [[Sam Lane (character)|Sam Lane]]: Father of Lois and grandfather of Jonathan and Jordan, a no-nonsense, workaholic army general who is determined to keep America and the world safe from all threats.<ref name="Walsh"/>
* [[Emmanuelle Chriqui]] as [[Lana Lang]]:<ref>{{cite web|last=Flook|first=Ray|title=Superman & Lois: Emmanuelle Chriqui's Finale Check-In; Tulloch's Gift|url=https://bleedingcool.com/tv/superman-tullochs-gift/|website=[[Bleeding Cool]]|date=April 15, 2024|access-date=April 15, 2024}}</ref><br />An old friend of Clark Kent and the former loan officer at Smallville Bank. In season two, she becomes the new mayor of Smallville.<ref name="Chriqui" /> Milano Hryshchenko portrays a childhood Lana, Sara Rizk portrays a grade school Lana, and Emma Newton portrays a teenage Lana.
* [[Tayler Buck]] as [[Natasha Irons|Natalie Lane Irons / Starlight]] (seasons 2–4;<ref name="Buck promoted"/> guest season 1): John Henry Irons's daughter from his Earth with an alternate version of Lois Lane.
* [[Sofia Hasmik]] as Chrissy Beppo (seasons 2–4;<ref name="Hasmik promoted"/> recurring season 1): A "go-getter" journalist at the ''Smallville Gazette'' who has a "chance encounter" that changes her life.<ref name="Hasmik" />
* [[Chad L. Coleman]] as [[Bruno Mannheim]] (seasons 3–4): The leader of [[Intergang]], the widower of the late [[Onomatopoeia (character)|Peia Mannheim]] and the father of Matteo Mannheim.<ref name="ChadLC"/>
* [[Michael Cudlitz]] as [[Lex Luthor (Arrowverse)|Lex Luthor]] (season 4{{efn|name="Cudlitz"|Cudlitz is listed among the main cast but receives "special appearance by" credit in the opening titles.}}; guest season 3):<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=2023-06-14 |title='Superman & Lois': Dylan Walsh & Emmanuelle Chriqui Among 7 Cast Members Not Returning, Michael Cudlitz Promoted To Regular For Season 4 |url=https://deadline.com/2023/06/superman-amp-lois-dylan-walsh-emmanuelle-chriqui-michael-cudlitz-promoted-regular-1235417430/ |access-date=2023-06-15 |website=Deadline Hollywood |language=en-US |archive-date=June 15, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230615003111/https://deadline.com/2023/06/superman-amp-lois-dylan-walsh-emmanuelle-chriqui-michael-cudlitz-promoted-regular-1235417430/ |url-status=live }}</ref> A business mogul who seeks revenge on Lois Lane and her family.

