== Production ==
=== Development ===
The series was announced in October 2019 with [[Todd Helbing]], [[Greg Berlanti]], [[Sarah Schechter (producer)|Sarah Schechter]] and [[Geoff Johns]] executive producing, and Helbing penning the script.<ref name="SeriesAnnouncement"/> On January 14, 2020, [[The CW]] officially ordered ''Superman & Lois'' to series.<ref name="SeriesOrder"/> The first season consisted of 15 episodes.<ref>{{cite press release|title=The CW Gives Early Renewals to 12 Current Series for Next Season|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2021/02/03/the-cw-gives-early-renewals-to-12-current-series-for-next-season-430113/20210203cw01/|publisher=[[The CW]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=February 3, 2021|access-date=February 3, 2021}}</ref> The series ''[[Everwood]]'' and ''[[Friday Night Lights (TV series)|Friday Night Lights]]'' served as inspirations for the show, given they were also family dramas. Helbing explained many aspects of ''Superman & Lois'' were approached as if it were a feature film, such as the aspect ratio, cinematography, and production design, saying "We are competing with shows on cable and streamers...we wanted to be able to do that and offer audiences something of equal quality".<ref name="DeadlineTCAFeb2021" /> In March 2021, The CW renewed the series for a second season.<ref name="S2Renewal"/> In March 2022, The CW renewed the series for a third season.<ref name="S3Renewal">{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2022/03/the-cw-renewals-the-flash-nancy-drew-kung-fu-1234984336/|title=The CW Renews Seven Scripted Series: 'The Flash', 'Kung Fu', 'All American', 'Nancy Drew', 'Superman & Lois', 'Walker' & 'Riverdale' Returning|website=Deadline Hollywood|first=Peter|last=White|date=March 22, 2022|access-date=March 22, 2022|archive-date=February 3, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210203211446/https://deadline.com/2022/03/the-cw-renewals-the-flash-nancy-drew-kung-fu-1234984336/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In January 2023, [[DC Studios]] CEOs [[James Gunn]] and [[Peter Safran]] said they expected the show to continue for "one to two more seasons".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Otterson |first=Joe |date=2023-01-31 |title='Superman & Lois' Has 'One or Two More Seasons Left,' New DC Studios Heads Say |url=https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/superman-and-lois-one-or-two-more-seasons-james-gunn-peter-safran-1235506971/ |access-date=2023-02-09 |website=Variety |archive-date=February 9, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230209121204/https://variety.com/2023/tv/news/superman-and-lois-one-or-two-more-seasons-james-gunn-peter-safran-1235506971/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Brad Schwartz, President of Entertainment at The CW, stated in May 2023 that the business model of the show was no longer feasible for the network due to the show being expensive to produce, adding that it did not directly generate any profits and The CW did not have the rights to previous seasons.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=2023-05-18 |title=Superhero Shows "Had Their Time" as New CW Leaders Outline Plans to Make Network "Bigger and Profitable" |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/nextar-pitches-cw-reinvention-less-superheroes-older-audience-1235495292/ |access-date=2023-06-09 |website=The Hollywood Reporter |archive-date=June 9, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230609201704/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/nextar-pitches-cw-reinvention-less-superheroes-older-audience-1235495292/ |url-status=live }}</ref> On June 12, 2023, The CW renewed the series for a fourth season consisting of ten episodes which was announced to be the last one on November 2, 2023. Under the renewal agreement, the series had the number of its regular cast members and writers as well as action scenes reduced while gearing more towards a family-focused drama in an effort to reduce production costs.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/superman-lois-all-american-homecoming-renewed-cw-1235513774/|title='Superman & Lois,' 'All American: Homecoming' Renewed, 'Gotham Knights' Canceled at The CW|publisher=The Hollywood Reporter|first=Lesley|last=Goldberg|date=June 12, 2023|access-date=June 12, 2023}}</ref><ref name="THRending">{{cite web|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/superman-and-lois-end-season-4-the-cw-dc-1235635904/|title=End of The CW's DC Era: 'Superman & Lois' to Conclude With Season 4|publisher=The Hollywood Reporter|first=Lesley|last=Goldberg|date=November 2, 2023|access-date=November 2, 2023|archive-date=November 2, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231102215024/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/superman-and-lois-end-season-4-the-cw-dc-1235635904/|url-status=live}}</ref> Production was however delayed due to the 2023 [[2023 Writers Guild of America strike|Writers Guild of America]] and [[2023 SAG-AFTRA strike|SAG-AFTRA]] strikes, with the season being scheduled for a 2024 fall-premiere.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hayes |first=Dade |date=August 8, 2023 |title=Strike Impact On The CW "Won't Hurt Our Forward Progress," Nexstar CEO Perry Sook Says: "We Kind Of Like Our Chances In This Chaotic Environment" |url=https://deadline.com/2023/08/the-cw-looking-like-fox-nexstar-ceo-perry-sook-sports-wga-sag-strike-1235457318/ |access-date=October 19, 2023 |website=Deadline Hollywood |archive-date=October 25, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231025203838/https://deadline.com/2023/08/the-cw-looking-like-fox-nexstar-ceo-perry-sook-sports-wga-sag-strike-1235457318/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://deadline.com/2024/02/all-american-homecoming-season-3-superman-lois-season-4-release-date-1235826869/|title='All American: Homecoming' Season 3 Likely To Debut In Summer On The CW; 'Superman & Lois' Final Season Headed To Fall|work=[[Deadline Hollywood]]|first=Katie|last=Campione|access-date=February 15, 2024|date=February 15, 2024|archive-date=March 3, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240303173617/https://deadline.com/2024/02/all-american-homecoming-season-3-superman-lois-season-4-release-date-1235826869/|url-status=live}}</ref> Schwartz stated in an interview that the decision to end the series was made by [[Warner Bros. Discovery]] to avoid competition with the upcoming [[DC Universe (franchise)|DC Universe]] (DCU) film ''[[Superman (2025 film)|Superman]]'' (2025).<ref>{{cite web|last1=Cobb|first1=Kayla|first2=Jose|last2=Alejandr Bastidas|title=CW's New Bosses Bet on Linear: 'We're Not in the SVOD Business'|url=https://www.thewrap.com/cw-brad-schwartz-dennis-miller-interview-linear-tv-strategy/|publisher=TheWrap|date=February 16, 2024|access-date=February 20, 2024}}</ref>

=== Casting ===
[[Tyler Hoechlin]] and [[Elizabeth Tulloch]] were signed on to reprise their roles as [[Clark Kent (Arrowverse)|Clark Kent]] and [[Lois Lane (Arrowverse)|Lois Lane]] from ''[[Supergirl (TV series)|Supergirl]]''.<ref name="SeriesAnnouncement">{{cite web |url=https://variety.com/2019/tv/news/superman-and-lois-series-tyler-hoechlin-elizabeth-tulloch-cw-1203385627/ |title='Superman and Lois' Starring Tyler Hoechlin, Elizabeth Tulloch in the Works at CW |last=Otterson |first=Joe |date=October 28, 2019 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200205214545/https://variety.com/2019/tv/news/superman-and-lois-series-tyler-hoechlin-elizabeth-tulloch-cw-1203385627/ |archive-date=February 5, 2020 |access-date=February 5, 2020}}</ref> In February 2020, Jordan Elsass and [[Alex Garfin]] were cast as Clark and Lois' sons Jonathan Kent and Jordan Kent, respectively.<ref name="ElsassGarfin" /> In April, [[Dylan Walsh]] was cast as [[Sam Lane (character)|Samuel Lane]]. Walsh replaces [[Glenn Morshower]], who previously recurred in the role on ''Supergirl''.<ref name="Walsh" /> [[Emmanuelle Chriqui]] was also cast as [[Lana Lang]],<ref name="Chriqui" /> along with [[Erik Valdez]] as Kyle Cushing.<ref name="Valdez"/> The next month, [[Wolé Parks]] was cast as "The Stranger" while [[Inde Navarrette]] was cast as Sarah Cushing.<ref name="Parks" /><ref name="Navarrette"/> Additionally, [[Adam Rayner]] portrays [[Morgan Edge (Arrowverse)|Morgan Edge]], who was previously portrayed by [[Adrian Pasdar]] in ''Supergirl''.<ref name="Rayner" />

In October 2020, [[Sofia Hasmik]] and [[Stacey Farber]] were cast in the recurring roles of Chrissy Beppo and Leslie Larr, respectively.<ref name="Hasmik" /><ref name="Farber" /> In December 2020, [[David Ramsey]] was revealed to be reprising his ''[[Arrow (TV series)|Arrow]]'' role of [[John Diggle (Arrowverse)|John Diggle]] in addition to directing at least one episode in the series.<ref name="Ramsey"/> In June 2021, Hasmik was promoted to a series regular for the second season.<ref name="Hasmik promoted"/> In August 2021, [[Tayler Buck]], who guest starred in the first season, was promoted to a series regular for the second season.<ref name="Buck promoted"/> In October 2021, [[Ian Bohen]] was cast in a recurring role as Lt. Mitch Anderson for the second season.<ref name="Bohen"/> [[Jenna Dewan]], who previously played Lucy Lane on ''Supergirl'' reprised her role in the second season.<ref>{{Cite web|date=October 29, 2021|title=Jenna Dewan to Reprise 'Supergirl' Role on 'Superman & Lois' (Exclusive)|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/jenna-dewan-supergirl-superman-lois-1235039112/|work=The Hollywood Reporter|first=LESLEY|last=GOLDBERG|access-date=October 29, 2021|archive-date=October 29, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211029174328/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/jenna-dewan-supergirl-superman-lois-1235039112/|url-status=live}}</ref>

In August 2022, Elsass departed the series ahead of the third season for personal reasons.<ref name="ElsassExits" /> The following month, his role was recast to Michael Bishop<ref name="Bishop" /> and [[Chad L. Coleman]] was cast as [[Bruno Mannheim]].<ref name="ChadLC">{{Cite web|date=September 14, 2022|title=Superman & Lois Casts The Orville's Chad L. Coleman as Intergang Head Bruno Mannheim for Season 3|url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/superman-and-lois-season-3-chad-l-coleman-bruno-mannheim-1234871926/|work=[[TVLine]]|first=Andy|last=Swift|access-date=September 19, 2022|url-status=live|archive-date=February 4, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230204064504/https://tvline.com/2022/09/14/superman-and-lois-season-3-chad-l-coleman-bruno-mannheim/}}</ref> [[Lex Luthor]] appears in the show where he is now portrayed by [[Michael Cudlitz]] instead of a reprisal from [[Jon Cryer]], who played his doppelgänger on Earth-Prime.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/superman-lois-lex-luthor-recast-michael-cudlitz-season-3-1234924822/|title=''Superman & Lois'' Casts Michael Cudlitz as New Lex Luthor for Season 3|work=TVLine|first=Andy|last=Swift|date=January 24, 2023|access-date=January 27, 2023|archive-date=January 26, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230126160610/https://tvline.com/2023/01/24/superman-lois-lex-luthor-recast-michael-cudlitz-season-3/|url-status=live}}</ref>

Seven of the twelve cast members were cut as series regulars following the renewal of the show for the fourth and final season. These included Dylan Walsh, Emmanuelle Chriqui, Erik Valdez, Inde Navarrette, Wolé Parks, Tayler Buck and Sofia Hasmik. Michael Cudlitz joins as a main cast member following his guest appearances in the previous season,<ref name=":0" /> receiving "special appearance by" credit.{{cn|date=October 2024}} Navarrette confirmed in July 2023 that she would return as a guest star for at least three episodes.<ref name="Holmes"/> Ultimately, each member of the supporting cast that appeared in the previous season reprised their role and retained main cast billing for the episodes that they appeared in.

=== Filming ===
Production on the pilot was expected to begin on March 23, 2020, in [[Vancouver, British Columbia]], and conclude on May 14.<ref name="PilotProductionDates"/> However, on March 13, 2020, plans to shoot a pilot were delayed due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic in the United States|COVID-19 pandemic]], to either June or July of that year.<ref name="PilotScrappedVariety"/><ref name="PilotScrappedTHR"/> In late July 2020, Warner Bros. Television planned for the Vancouver-based production to restart in late August.<ref name="ProductionRestartDates"/> Filming of season 1 began on October 21, 2020, and concluded on July 2, 2021.<ref name="FilmingDates"/><ref>{{cite web|title=Filming Concludes on Season 1 of "Superman & Lois"|url=https://www.supermanhomepage.com/filming-concludes-on-season-1-of-superman-lois/|website=Superman Homepage|date=July 2, 2021|access-date=July 2, 2021|archive-date=July 2, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210702123117/https://www.supermanhomepage.com/filming-concludes-on-season-1-of-superman-lois/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite tweet|user=BitsieTulloch|first=Elizabeth|last=Tulloch|number=1410971717153923072|title=That's a wrap on season 1|date=July 2, 2021|access-date=July 7, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210705202439/https://twitter.com/bitsietulloch/status/1410971717153923072|archive-date=July 5, 2021|url-status=live}}</ref> The series is filmed on location in [[Surrey, British Columbia]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.vancouverisawesome.com/vancouver-news/15-million-smallville-surrey-2778281|title=$1.5-million Smallville constructed in Surrey for new TV series (PHOTOS)|last=Grochowski|first=Sarah|work=Vancouver is Awesome|date=October 8, 2020|access-date=April 27, 2021|archive-date=November 16, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201116190837/https://www.vancouverisawesome.com/vancouver-news/15-million-smallville-surrey-2778281|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://globalnews.ca/news/7384389/superman-and-lois-surrey/|title=New 'Superman and Lois' TV series to be filmed in Surrey, B.C.|last=Azpiri|first=Jon|work=Global News|date=October 7, 2020|access-date=April 27, 2021|archive-date=October 22, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201022064416/https://globalnews.ca/news/7384389/superman-and-lois-surrey/|url-status=live}}</ref> The second season began filming on September 15, 2021, and concluded on May 5, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 20, 2022 |title=DGC BC Production List |url=https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Production/Production-List.pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220520195445/https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Production/Production-List.pdf |archive-date=May 20, 2022 |access-date=May 20, 2022 |website=[[Directors Guild of Canada]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite tweet|user=BitsieTulloch|author=Bitsie Tulloch|number=1437804506733891586|title=Day one, Season Two! #SupermanAndLois|date=September 15, 2021|access-date=October 2, 2021|archive-date=September 15, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210915012827/https://twitter.com/BitsieTulloch/status/1437804506733891586|url-status=live}}</ref> Filming of the third season began on September 6, 2022<ref>{{cite web |last1=Flook |first1=Ray |title=Superman & Lois S03: Elizabeth Tulloch Had "Great First Week Back" |url=https://bleedingcool.com/tv/superman-lois-s03-elizabeth-tulloch-had-great-first-week-back/ |website=Bleeding Cool |access-date=September 13, 2022 |date=September 9, 2022 |archive-date=September 13, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220913040650/https://bleedingcool.com/tv/superman-lois-s03-elizabeth-tulloch-had-great-first-week-back/ |url-status=live }}</ref> in Vancouver, and concluded on March 14, 2023.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Production/Production-List.pdf |title=DGC BC Production List |work=[[Directors Guild of Canada]] |date=March 17, 2023 |access-date=March 17, 2023 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230317214652/https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Production/Production-List.pdf |archive-date=March 17, 2023}}</ref> Filming for the fourth season began on January 11, 2024 and concluded on April 24, 2024 with Hoechlin receiving a supportive letter from upcoming Superman actor [[David Corenswet]] as production wrapped up.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Baala |first=Sara |date=January 12, 2024 |title=Superman and Lois season four shares exciting filming update |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/ustv/a46367691/superman-and-lois-season-four-update/ |access-date=February 1, 2024 |work=[[Digital Spy]] |archive-date=January 19, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240119033455/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/ustv/a46367691/superman-and-lois-season-four-update/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Cooper |first=Alison |date=December 29, 2023 |title=9 movies and TV shows filming in Vancouver in January |url=https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/9-movies-tv-shows-filming-vancouver-jan-2024 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240206043328/https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/9-movies-tv-shows-filming-vancouver-jan-2024 |archive-date=February 6, 2024 |access-date=February 6, 2024 |work=[[Daily Hive]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mishra |first=Shrishty |date=April 24, 2024 |title='Superman & Lois' Wraps Filming on Its Series Finale |url=https://collider.com/superman-and-lois-final-season-filming-wrap/ |access-date=April 27, 2024 |work=[[Collider (website)|Collider]] |url-status=live |archive-date=May 1, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240501025539/https://collider.com/superman-and-lois-final-season-filming-wrap/ }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Burlingame |first=Russ |date=April 24, 2024 |title=Superman & Lois Wraps Production on Series Finale |url=https://comicbook.com/tv-shows/news/superman-lois-wraps-production-on-series-finale/ |access-date=April 27, 2024 |work=ComicBook.com |url-status=live |archive-date=April 27, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240427233751/https://comicbook.com/tv-shows/news/superman-lois-wraps-production-on-series-finale/ }}</ref><ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?si=_12Qrv8TOBXqupts&t=508&v=SoKbEO_1se8&feature=youtu.be |title='Superman & Lois' Stars on Passing the Torch to David Corenswet & Rachel Brosnahan {{!}} Comic-Con 2024 |date=2024-07-27 |last=The Hollywood Reporter |access-date=2024-12-05 |via=YouTube}}</ref> The cast and crew held a [[Wrap (filmmaking)|wrap party]] on April 25, 2024 to celebrate the conclusion of four seasons of filming.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Behbakht |first=Andy |date=April 24, 2024 |title=Superman & Lois Officially Wraps Filming As Lois Lane Actress Confirms Completion Of The CW's Final DC TV Show |url=https://screenrant.com/superman-lois-season-4-filming-end-confirm/ |access-date=April 27, 2024 |work=[[Screen Rant]] |url-status=live |archive-date=April 28, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240428040806/https://screenrant.com/superman-lois-season-4-filming-end-confirm/ }}</ref>

=== Writing ===
In November 2020, series writer Nadria Tucker announced she was fired from the show, claiming it was for "pushing back on racist and sexist storylines." She also claimed she worked on all 15 episodes of the first season, but was only paid for 13 of them.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Daniels|first=Karu F.|title=Black 'Superman & Lois' writer Nadria Tucker opens up about being fired after pushing back on racist and sexist storylines|url=https://www.nydailynews.com/2021/03/03/black-superman-lois-writer-nadria-tucker-opens-up-about-being-fired-after-pushing-back-on-racist-and-sexist-storylines/|access-date=April 9, 2021|website=New York Daily News|date=March 3, 2021|archive-date=April 14, 2021|url-access=limited|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210414110811/https://www.nydailynews.com/snyde/ny-superman-and-lois-nadria-tucker-fired-racist-sexist-storylines-20210304-dlxpiymzhraldce76rcete7xnq-story.html|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title='Superman & Lois' Writer Nadria Tucker Says She Was Fired After Raising Issues With CW Show's Sexism and Racism|url=https://www.slashfilm.com/superman-lois-writer-cw-issues/|access-date=April 9, 2021|website=/Film|author=Bui, Hoai-Tran|date=November 9, 2020|archive-date=April 14, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210414082035/https://www.slashfilm.com/superman-lois-writer-cw-issues/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Ex-Superman & Lois Writer: "I Can't Say I Felt Heard"; Fisher/JL Case|url=https://bleedingcool.com/tv/ex-superman-fisher-jl-case/|access-date=April 9, 2021|website=bleedingcool.com|author=Flook, Ray|date=February 28, 2021|archive-date=April 14, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210414203934/https://bleedingcool.com/tv/ex-superman-fisher-jl-case/|url-status=live}}</ref> In a statement, WBTV claimed that "Warner Bros. Television did not exercise its option to extend her [contract] for additional episodes" and that "WBTV was transparent and told her why it was not picking up her option."<ref>{{Cite web|title=Nadria Tucker Discusses 'Seemingly Out of Nowhere' Dismissal From Superman & Lois Writers' Room and WB Investigation [Updated]|url=https://thegrapevine.theroot.com/nadria-tucker-discusses-seemingly-out-of-nowhere-dismis-1846456451|access-date=April 29, 2021|website=The Grapevine|date=March 3, 2021|author=Stidhum, Tonja Renee|archive-date=April 29, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210429170150/https://thegrapevine.theroot.com/nadria-tucker-discusses-seemingly-out-of-nowhere-dismis-1846456451|url-status=live}}</ref>

== Connection to the Arrowverse ==
Speaking of the lack of greater [[Arrowverse]] connections in the first season, showrunner [[Aaron and Todd Helbing|Todd Helbing]] felt that there was "this weird set of circumstances where, because of production or timing or COVID, everything in the show that was related to the Arrowverse has gotten pulled out". He added that, as development progressed further away from the "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths]]" crossover, "it felt like we were opening a can of worms every time we had to explain the connection", though he was hopeful more connections or proper crossovers could occur in the second season.<ref>{{cite web |last=Swift |first=Andy |date=May 18, 2021 |title=Superman & Lois EP Reveals Supergirl Easter Egg You Didn't See This Season |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/supergirl-superman-and-lois-season-1-cancelled-crossover-moment-1234673631/ |access-date=May 18, 2021 |website=[[TVLine]] |archive-date=May 20, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210520130428/https://tvline.com/2021/05/18/supergirl-superman-and-lois-season-1-cancelled-crossover-moment/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Though the multiverse, [[Oliver Queen (Arrowverse)|Oliver Queen]] and the Arrowverse's version of the League{{Efn|Informally established at the end of the "Crisis on Infinite Earths" crossover, although the term "Justice League" has never been mentioned in-universe.}} were mentioned in the first season, the second season finale establishes that the series takes place adjacent to Earth-Prime, with different iterations of the characters compared to their Earth-Prime counterparts and a different continuity with Superman being that Earth's only hero, though the change of setting itself is never fully explained. Helbing later revealed that the show's setting was separate from Earth-Prime, a decision he and [[DC Entertainment]] made. He further added that the Superman, Lois Lane, Lucy Lane and John Diggle in the series are doppelgangers of the ones on Earth-Prime.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Swift |first=Andy |date=June 29, 2022 |title=How Is Superman & Lois Connected to the Arrowverse? EP Sheds More Light on Finale's Long-Awaited Explanation |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/superman-lois-arrowverse-connection-explained-finale-interview-1234846652/ |access-date=June 29, 2022 |website=TVLine |archive-date=June 29, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220629010235/https://tvline.com/2022/06/28/superman-lois-arrowverse-connection-explained-finale-interview/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

== Release ==
=== Broadcast ===
''Superman & Lois'' premiered on The CW on February 23, 2021.<ref name="SeriesPremiereDate"/> After a delay in production caused by COVID-19, the series went on hiatus after the fifth episode, during which the [[Supergirl (season 6)|sixth and final season]] of ''[[Supergirl (TV series)|Supergirl]]'' took over the series' timeslot.<ref>{{Cite web |last=White |first=Peter |date=March 5, 2021 |title='Superman & Lois' Temporally Moves Off The CW Schedule Due To Previous Covid-19 Pause, 'Supergirl' Flies into Help |url=https://deadline.com/2021/03/superman-lois-the-cw-schedule-supergirl-1234707899/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210305195509/https://deadline.com/2021/03/superman-lois-the-cw-schedule-supergirl-1234707899/ |archive-date=March 5, 2021 |access-date=March 5, 2021 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The second season premiered on January 11, 2022.<ref name="Season2Regulars">{{Cite web|last=Swift|first=Andy|date=June 30, 2021|title=''Superman & Lois'' Ups Sofia Hasmik to Series Regular Ahead of Season 2|url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/superman-and-lois-season-2-sofia-hasmik-promoted-chrissy-beppo-1234694904/|access-date=August 10, 2021|website=TVLine|archive-date=August 10, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210810221820/https://tvline.com/2021/06/30/superman-and-lois-season-2-sofia-hasmik-promoted-chrissy-beppo/|url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="S2Prem">{{cite web|url=https://www.tvline.com/news/superman-and-lois-season-2-premiere-date-cw-midseason-schedule-1234740452/|title=The CW's Midseason Schedule Teams ''Superman & Lois'' With ''Naomi'', Sets ''Dynasty'', ''Charmed'' and ''Kung Fu'' Returns|last=Mitovich|first=Matt Webb|work=TVLine|date=November 5, 2021|access-date=November 5, 2021|archive-date=November 5, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211105180247/https://tvline.com/2021/11/05/superman-and-lois-season-2-premiere-date-cw-midseason-schedule/|url-status=live}}</ref> The third season premiered on March 14, 2023.<ref name="S3Premiere">{{Cite web |last=Pedersen |first=Erik |date=December 14, 2022 |title='Gotham Knights', 'Superman & Lois' Season 3 Premiere Dates Set At The CW|url=https://deadline.com/2022/12/gotham-knights-premiere-date-superman-lois-season-3-date-the-cw-1235199275/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221214200951/https://deadline.com/2022/12/gotham-knights-premiere-date-superman-lois-season-3-date-the-cw-1235199275/ |archive-date=December 14, 2022 |access-date=December 14, 2022 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The fourth and final season premiered on October 7, 2024.<ref name="S4Premiere">{{Cite web |last=Petski |first=Denise |date=June 20, 2024 |title=The CW Sets Fall Premiere Dates For Final Season Of 'Superman & Lois', 'WWE NXT', 'Sullivan's Crossing', 'The Chosen' & More |url=https://deadline.com/2024/06/the-cw-fall-premiere-dates-superman-and-lois-wwe-nxt-sullivans-crossing-the-chosen-1235978853/|url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240620160831/https://deadline.com/2024/06/the-cw-fall-premiere-dates-superman-and-lois-wwe-nxt-sullivans-crossing-the-chosen-1235978853/ |archive-date=June 20, 2024 |access-date=June 20, 2024 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref name="Final Season Premiere Date Change">{{Cite press release|title=The CW Network Sets New Fall Premiere Dates for "Scrabble," "Trivial Pursuit," "Superman & Lois" and "The Wranglers"|url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/news/2024/08/29/the-cw-network-sets-new-fall-premiere-dates-for-scrabble-trivial-pursuit-superman-and-lois-and-the-wranglers-957511/20240829cw02/|publisher=[[The CW]]|via=[[The Futon Critic]]|date=August 29, 2024}}</ref>

[[CTV Sci-Fi Channel]] aired the series in Canada.<ref>{{cite press release|url=https://www.bellmedia.ca/the-lede/press/the-man-of-steel-soars-to-ctv-sci-fi-channel-with-premiere-of-all-new-series-superman-lois-february-23/|title=The Man of Steel Soars to CTV Sci-Fi Channel with Premiere of All-New Series, SUPERMAN & LOIS, February 23|work=[[Bell Media]]|location=Toronto|date=February 5, 2021|access-date=February 19, 2021|archive-date=February 15, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210215062646/https://www.bellmedia.ca/the-lede/press/the-man-of-steel-soars-to-ctv-sci-fi-channel-with-premiere-of-all-new-series-superman-lois-february-23/|url-status=live}}</ref> The [[BBC]] acquired the [[United Kingdom|UK]] broadcast rights to the show. The series premiered on [[BBC One]] on December 4, 2021, and was made available to stream on [[BBC iPlayer]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=November 16, 2021|title=BBC ACQUIRES SUPERHERO DRAMA SUPERMAN & LOIS|url=https://www.tvzoneuk.com/post/bbc-supermanloid|work=TV Zone|access-date=November 16, 2021|archive-date=November 16, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211116161434/https://www.tvzoneuk.com/post/bbc-supermanloid|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Home media ===
Beginning March 5, 2021, extended versions of episodes of ''Superman & Lois'' started streaming on The CW's app and website a day after the release of an episode.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://comicbook.com/dc/news/superman-lois-extended-episodes-coming-to-cw-app/|title=Superman & Lois Extended Episodes Coming to CW App|author=Russ Burlingame|work=ComicBook.com|publisher=[[ViacomCBS]]|date=March 5, 2021|access-date=August 24, 2022|archive-date=August 24, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220824115144/https://comicbook.com/dc/news/superman-lois-extended-episodes-coming-to-cw-app/|url-status=live}}</ref> The entire first season became available on [[HBO Max]] on September 17, 2021.<ref name= "HBO Max">{{Cite web|date=September 17, 2021|title="Superman & Lois" Season 1 Now Available on HBO Max|url=https://www.supermanhomepage.com/superman-lois-season-1-now-available-on-hbo-max/|access-date=September 18, 2021|work=Superman Homepage|archive-date=September 18, 2021|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210918062603/https://www.supermanhomepage.com/superman-lois-season-1-now-available-on-hbo-max/|url-status=live}}</ref> The second season was made available on July 29, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|date=June 29, 2022|title=The Best New Shows on HBO Max (July 2022)|url=https://www.cbr.com/best-new-shows-hbo-max-july-2022/|work=Comic Book Resources|first=Katie|last=Doll|access-date=August 14, 2022|archive-date=July 8, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220708121333/https://www.cbr.com/best-new-shows-hbo-max-july-2022/|url-status=live}}</ref> The third season was released on the rebranded Max streaming service on July 28, 2023.<ref>{{Cite web|date=June 26, 2023|title=Superman & Lois Season 3 Streaming Release Date Announced by Max|url=https://thedirect.com/article/superman-and-lois-season-3-streaming-release-date-max|work=The Direct|first=Aeron|last=Mer Eclarinal|access-date=June 28, 2023|archive-date=June 28, 2023|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230628081655/https://thedirect.com/article/superman-and-lois-season-3-streaming-release-date-max|url-status=live}}</ref> The fourth season was released on January 1, 2025.<ref>{{Cite web|date=January 1, 2025|title=HBO and Max New Releases: January 2025|url=https://www.denofgeek.com/tv/hbo-and-max-new-releases-january-2025/|work=Den of Greek|first=Brynna|last=Arens|access-date=February 22, 2025}}</ref>

Season one of the series was released on Blu-ray and DVD in the U.S. on October 19, 2021.<ref>{{Cite web|title=New Releases: Oct. 19, 2021|url=https://www.mediaplaynews.com/research/new-releases-oct-19-2021/|date=October 19, 2021|access-date=August 24, 2022|work=Media Play News|archive-date=August 24, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220824114101/https://www.mediaplaynews.com/research/new-releases-oct-19-2021/|url-status=live}}</ref> Season two was released on September 27, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|date=September 27, 2022|title=New Releases: September 27, 2022|url=https://www.mediaplaynews.com/research/new-releases-sept-27-2022/|work=Media Play News|access-date=October 31, 2022|archive-date=October 31, 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221031183000/https://www.mediaplaynews.com/research/new-releases-sept-27-2022/|url-status=live}}</ref> The third season was released on June 11, 2024.<ref>{{Cite web|date=June 11, 2024|title=New Releases: June 11, 2024|url=https://www.mediaplaynews.com/research/new-releases-june-11-2024/|work=Media Play News|access-date=December 21, 2022}}</ref> The fourth season as well as the complete series was released on April 1, 2025.<ref>{{Cite news|title=New Releases: April 1, 2025|url=https://www.mediaplaynews.com/research/new-releases-april-1-2025/|publisher=Media Play News|date=April 1, 2025|access-date=April 16, 2025}}</ref>

== Reception ==
=== Critical response ===
On [[Rotten Tomatoes]], the series has an approval rating of 88%, with an average rating of 7.8/10. The website's critical consensus reads "Though it may be a bit too grounded for some viewers, ''Superman & Lois'' draws strength from unexpected places{{snd}}without skimping on the action{{snd}}to carve its own path in a crowded superhero universe."<ref>{{Cite web|title=Superman & Lois|url=https://www.rottentomatoes.com/tv/superman_and_lois|access-date=June 15, 2024|website=[[Rotten Tomatoes]]|language=en}}</ref> On [[Metacritic]], it has a weighted average score of 65 out of 100 based on 18 reviews, indicating "generally favorable reviews".<ref>{{Cite Metacritic|id=superman-lois|title=Superman & Lois|type=tv|access-date=July 9, 2026|publisher_hide=y}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

